# 🔧 wtfix — *What The Fix?*

**AI-powered terminal error analyzer. Wrap any failing command and get instant, actionable solutions — right in your terminal.**

[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.9%2B-blue?logo=python&logoColor=white)](https://www.python.org/)
[![Gemini](https://img.shields.io/badge/Powered%20by-Gemini%202.5%20Flash-8A2BE2?logo=google&logoColor=white)](https://deepmind.google/technologies/gemini/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Rich](https://img.shields.io/badge/Terminal%20UI-Rich-ff69b4)](https://github.com/Textualize/rich)
[![Typer](https://img.shields.io/badge/CLI-Typer-009688)](https://typer.tiangolo.com/)

---

</div>

## ✨ What is wtfix?

`wtfix` is a zero-friction CLI tool that sits between you and your errors. It captures `stderr`, sends it to **Google Gemini 2.5 Flash**, and prints a crisp, structured diagnosis — no copy-pasting into ChatGPT, no Googling stack traces.

---

## 🚀 Features

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| 🎯 **Subprocess mode** | Wrap any command: `wtfix python app.py` |
| 🪄 **Pipe/stdin mode** | `cat error.log \| wtfix` |
| 🤖 **Gemini 2.5 Flash** | Fast, smart, cost-effective analysis |
| 🎨 **Rich terminal UI** | Spinner, panels, syntax-highlighted output |
| 📋 **3-point report** | Root cause → Why it happened → Copy-paste fix |
| 🌐 **Language agnostic** | Python, Node.js, Go, Rust, Docker, Bash … |
| ⚡ **Zero config** | One env var, one install — done |

---

## 📦 Installation

### 1 — Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/erenbezgin/wtfix.git
cd wtfix
```

### 2 — Install in editable mode

```bash
pip install -e .
```

The `wtfix` command is now available system-wide.

### 3 — Set your Gemini API key

Get a **free** API key at [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey).

```bash
# Linux / macOS
export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"

# Windows PowerShell
$env:GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key-here"

# Windows CMD
set GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
```

> **Tip:** Add the export line to your `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc` so it persists across sessions.

---

## 🎬 Usage

### Mode 1 — Subprocess (wrap a command)

```bash
wtfix python tests/broken_app.py
wtfix npm run build
wtfix go build ./...
wtfix cargo build
wtfix docker compose up
```

```
╭─ Running command ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ $ python tests/broken_app.py                                                 │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ stderr output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Traceback (most recent call last):                                           │
│   File "tests/broken_app.py", line 4, in <module>                           │
│     import nonexistent_module                                                │
│ ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'nonexistent_module'                   │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

⚡ Analysing stderr with Gemini gemini-2.5-flash…

⠸ Thinking

╭─ 🤖 wtfix — AI Analysis ────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│ ## 1. 🔍 Hatanın Özü (Ne patladı?)                                          │
│ Python could not find the module `nonexistent_module` at import time.        │
│                                                                              │
│ ## 2. 💡 Neden Kaynaklandı? (Satır, dosya ve mantık hatası)                 │
│ Line 4 of `tests/broken_app.py` tries to import `nonexistent_module`,       │
│ which is not installed in the current Python environment.                    │
│                                                                              │
│ ## 3. 🛠️ Çözüm Adımı                                                       │
│ ```bash                                                                      │
│ pip install nonexistent_module                                               │
│ ```                                                                          │
│ If the module name is a typo, correct the import statement instead.          │
│                                                                              │
╰────────────────────────── Powered by Gemini 2.5 Flash ──────────────────────╯
```

### Mode 2 — Pipe (stdin)

```bash
# Pipe a saved log file
cat error.log | wtfix

# Pipe both stdout and stderr from a command
python app.py 2>&1 | wtfix

# Combine commands
npm run build 2>&1 | wtfix
```

### Getting help

```bash
wtfix --help
wtfix --version
```

